  "description": "MOZJAQ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C136 H160 Dy6 N20 O25 P4,3(C2 H3 N1),2(C3 H7 N1 O1),3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.715-3.927 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.89-114.80°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C148H189Dy6N25O30P4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
